<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- One UI on SM-S948B, Probe display/framework_res.txt, 2026-10-27.
     v2 (2026-10-27): v1 bound into /oem but status bar still too high in the
     setup wizard photo, so v2 overrides status_bar_height DIRECTLY (not only
     via its portrait reference) and status_bar_height_default to the same mm
     value, to remove any fallback reading default (30dp) or a reference that
     does not propagate. Priority raised 1 -> 10 so this overlay wins over
     product overlays (GoogleConfig priority 0) on any tie.
     Navigation: Pixel framework config_navBarInteractionMode is 0 (3-button)
     in framework-res; the guest shows a 3-button triangle that the setup
     wizard Accept card overlaps. v2 sets gesture mode (2, Pixel default) so
     the triangle bar is gone and Accept sits above the gesture bar as on a
     real Pixel. navigation_bar_height is kept explicit at 48dp so switching
     back to 3-button in Settings still gets a correct inset.
     v3 (2026-10-27, measured): home status bar icons sit 20 image px
     (22 phone px) above lock screen icons (home centre 47, lock centre 67,
     camera centre 64 in screenshot px), so home icons sit above the camera
     hole while lock icons align with it. Raising framework height by
     ~42 phone px moves a centred icon down ~21 phone px, matching lock.
     9.68mm = 7.54mm + 42px at ~19.7 px/mm. The SystemUI statusbar overlay
     pins status_bar_header_height_keyguard to 7.54mm in the same build, so
     the lock screen height does NOT follow this increase and stays put.
     Raising framework height alone would move both screens together and
     keep the 20px gap.
     v4 (2026-10-27, measured after v3): v3 overshot. Home centre moved
     47 -> 87 image px (ratio ~1.0 with height), lock centre moved
     67 -> 86 (ratio ~0.5, so the keyguard pin did NOT hold lock), QS
     centre 88. All three now sit ~23 image px (25 phone px) BELOW camera
     centre 64. To bring home back to camera, reduce height by 25 phone
     px = 1.28mm: 9.68 - 1.28 = 8.40mm. Home should land ~65 image px,
     lock ~76 (still below camera, because pin did not hold, but closer
     than 86).
     v5 (2026-10-27, measured after v4): v4 landed at centre 74-75 image
     px, not 65 as the 1:1 model predicted. The centred model holds
     instead: centre = height/2, v3 height 191px gave centre 95px,
     v4 height 165px gave centre 83px in theory but 74-75 measured
     (close to OneUI centre 76 in the same scale, 1-2px off). User still
     sees v4 as a bit low, not balanced with camera centre 64. To raise
     centre by ~10 image px (11 phone px), reduce height by ~22 phone
     px (centred model: 2x centre delta) = 1.22mm: 8.40 - 1.22 = 7.18mm,
     rounded to 7.20mm. Predicted centre ~65 image px, inside the
     pre-v3 lock range (67) the user called ok.
     v6 (2026-10-27, measured after v5): v5 home centre 63-64, lock centre
     67 (both image px, screenshots 16:35). User chooses home = lock, i.e.
     home down to 67. Home down 3-4 image px (3.8 phone px) needs height
     up 2x = 7.6 phone px = 0.39mm: 7.20 + 0.39 = 7.59mm, rounded to
     7.60mm. Predicted home ~67. Lock may also move down a little with
     height (lock pin did not hold in v3), so measure both again after
     v6; home = lock exactly is not guaranteed by framework height alone. -->
<resources>
    <dimen name="status_bar_height">7.60mm</dimen>
    <dimen name="status_bar_height_portrait">7.60mm</dimen>
    <dimen name="status_bar_height_default">7.60mm</dimen>
    <dimen name="navigation_bar_height">48dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="navigation_bar_height_landscape">48dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="navigation_bar_frame_height">48dp</dimen>
    <integer name="config_navBarInteractionMode">2</integer>
</resources>
